  "metadata": {
    "title": "Nilpotent-free spaces of 3 x 3 matrices over the field with three elements",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23607867",
    "publication_date": "2026-10-24",
    "description": "<p>We prove that the maximum dimension of a nilpotent-free linear subspace of M_3(F_3) is five, disproving the universally quantified finite-field assertion in Wigderson, arXiv:2609.29177v1, Conjecture 8. This submission revision includes a direct algebraic proof of the five-dimensional example, an exhaustive upper-bound coverage argument, a complete independent C verifier, a vector diagram and precise computational trust disclosure. The accompanying Lean development uses two native_decide evaluations for the finite upper bound; it is not a standard-axioms-only kernel proof. The new written algebraic and quadratic-form arguments are not claimed to be formalized. The manuscript is formatted for possible submission to Annals of Mathematics; it has not been submitted to or accepted by that journal. Source and verification files: https://github.com/creelie/Paper_2 . Original preprint: https://hexagonmath.org/2610.00480v1 .</p>",
